}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 You can use the <Menu> key to select a few other options.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 The graph is initially based on default figures for realistic use. The Revo is capable of running about 12.5 hours, provided that you leave it on and don't press any keys (!) but 9hrs is more typical.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 The light grey line shows the average current and is preset to 42mA.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 The sloping diagonal plot shows a dark grey 3 pixel line for the region exceeding your last peak charge volts.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 The plot changes to black for the monitored zone since your last charge.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 The plot switches to a dark grey, 1 pixel thick line for the predicted remaining time.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 Over time, the values used will accurately reflect your most recent usage characteristics and will allow you to assess the best time to recharge your Revo based on the way you use it and the real condition of your batteries.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \b Important\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 For ChaDis to be effective, it has to remain running in the background so it has been designed to stay running even if it receives a 'Close Program' message from the system screen or when you backup or install other programs using PsiWin. It is therefore r}{\f1 \fs20 ecommended that you Backup your Revo once while ChaDis is }{\f1 \fs20 \b \ul not}{\f1 \fs20  running. On subsequent backups when ChaDis}{\f1 \fs20 \b  }{\f1 \fs20 \b \ul is}{\f1 \fs20  running, you will see PsiWin making three unsuccessful attempts to close ChaDis before continuing as normal.\par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 To close ChaDis you can select 'Close' from its own menu, type <Ctrl-E> as usual while it is displaying its graph, or in an emergency, 'Kill' it from the System list of running programs (press a shift key while tapping the 'Close File' button).\par 
